> On Sat, Feb 07, 2015 at 09:23:38AM +0300, Gleki Arxokuna wrote:
> > Sorry but if you don't understand Lojban then ... why all this
> discussion here?
> > I was trying to show how Lojban parsers deal with another level of
> analysing text.
>
> Because And tried to make sense out of your trollish explanation w.r.t.
> English.
>

This explanation wasn't trollish. I truly believe that there is some
misunderstanding of how English text can be parsed, namely, that clauses
should not be necessarily attached to explicitly defined heads. Imprecise
numbers like {mo'e zo'e} could be used for parsing English as well.

And if And can't read Lojban sentences then a true comparison between
parsers for the two languages can't be made.

Is there anything more simple?
To talk about a subject one needs to be familiar with this subject.

Otherwise this reminds of "200 words for snow in Inuktitut".



>
> As this failed, I don't see any sense in further contributions to this
> thread..
>

That someone disagrees with you doesn't immediately mean he is not right.



